      "name": null,
      "problem": "The axis of symmetry of the parabola $y=k{x}^{2}+3x-15$ is $x=4.$ Find the value of $k.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we will calculate the axis of symmetry in terms of $k.$ Then, we will set our result equal to $4.$ \n\nThe equation of the axis of symmetry of the parabola $y=a{x}^{2}+bx+c$ is given by\n\n$$\nx=-\\frac{b}{2a}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $a=k$ and $b=3$ into the formula for the axis of symmetry, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =-\\frac{3}{2(k)} \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{2k}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe already know that the axis of symmetry is $x=4,$ so we must have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{3}{2k} & =4 \\\\ -3 & =8k \\\\ k & =-\\frac{3}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
